\t<\/div>\r\n\t\t\t<div class='fca_qc_score_container' style='display:none;'><div class='fca_qc_score_text'>You got {{SCORE_CORRECT}} out of {{SCORE_TOTAL}} <\/div><div class='fca_qc_score_title'><\/div><img class='fca_qc_score_img' src=''><div class='fca_qc_score_desc'><\/div><\/div> \r\n\t\t\t\r\n\t\t\t<div class='fca_qc_quiz_footer' style='display: none;'>\r\n\t\t\t\t<span class='fca_qc_question_count'><\/span>\t\t\r\n\t\t\t<\/div>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\r\n\t\t\t<div class='fca_qc_your_answer_container' style='display:none;'><p class='fca_qc_your_answers_text'>Your Answers<\/p><div class='fca_qc_insert_response_above'><\/div><\/div> \r\n\t\t\t\r\n\t\t\t\r\n\t\t\t\r\n\t\t<\/div>\r\n\t\t\n<\/div>\n<div class=\"su-tabs-pane su-u-clearfix su-u-trim\" data-title=\"Gettysburg\">\n<p>Gettysburg, Pennsylvania may be a very small town but it is full of history. Walking through the old streets, it is almost like you have traveled back in time. Definitely worth the visit!<br \/>\n<style type=\"text\/css\">\r\n\t#foogallery-gallery-3349 .fg-image {\r\n        width: 150px;\r\n    }\r\n<\/style>\r\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"foogallery foogallery-container foogallery-default foogallery-lightbox-foobox fg-gutter-10 fg-center fg-default fg-light fg-border-thin fg-shadow-outline fg-loading-default fg-loaded-fade-in fg-hover-fade fg-hover-zoom fg-ready\" id=\"foogallery-gallery-3349\" data-foogallery=\"{&quot;item&quot;:{&quot;showCaptionTitle&quot;:true,&quot;showCaptionDescription&quot;:true},&quot;lazy&quot;:true}\" >\r\n\t<div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.ibafflatusdesign.space\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/07\/20180525_133615-1.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"The Jennie Wade house is located on the outskirts of town, next to what are now several cemeteries. The house accommodated two families at the time: Georgia Anna Wade McClellan&#039;s family (i.e. Jennie Wade&#039;s sister&#039;s family) on the left and another on the right. While this was not her home, the house is named after Jennie Wade as this is where she died. She is depicted carrying bread and water to remind viewers of her efforts in the Civil War.\" data-attachment-id=\"4038\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"The Jennie Wade house is located on the outskirts of town, next to what are now several cemeteries. The house accommodated two families at the time: Georgia Anna Wade McClellan&#039;s family (i.e. Jennie Wade&#039;s sister&#039;s family) on the left and another on the right. While this was not her home, the house is named after Jennie Wade as this is where she died. She is depicted carrying bread and water to remind viewers of her efforts in the Civil War.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/www.ibafflatusdesign.space\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2018\/07\/20180525_133615-1\/152751021.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">The Jennie Wade house is located on the outskirts of town, next to what are now several cemeteries. The house accommodated two families at the time: Georgia Anna Wade McClellan's family (i.e. Jennie Wade's sister's family) on the left and another on the right. While this was not her home, the house is named after Jennie Wade as this is where she died. She is depicted carrying bread and water to remind viewers of her efforts in the Civil War.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.ibafflatusdesign.space\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/07\/20180525_123358.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"This is the living room of the Jennie Wade house. It is furnished as it was at the time of Jennie Wade&#039;s death. There is a bed in the living room as her sister, Georgia, had just given birth and was under bed rest. As a result, their mother left Jennie, her brother and a boy in their care in the family house near the center of the city to go take care of Georgia in this house. However, as the gunshots drew near, Jennie decided to join her mother and sister. So, she closed up their house and walked over with her brother and the other boy.\" data-attachment-id=\"4026\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"This is the living room of the Jennie Wade house. It is furnished as it was at the time of Jennie Wade&#039;s death. There is a bed in the living room as her sister, Georgia, had just given birth and was under bed rest. As a result, their mother left Jennie, her brother and a boy in their care in the family house near the center of the city to go take care of Georgia in this house. However, as the gunshots drew near, Jennie decided to join her mother and sister. So, she closed up their house and walked over with her brother and the other boy.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/www.ibafflatusdesign.space\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2018\/07\/20180525_123358\/3529135811.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">This is the living room of the Jennie Wade house. It is furnished as it was at the time of Jennie Wade's death. There is a bed in the living room as her sister, Georgia, had just given birth and was under bed rest. As a result, their mother left Jennie, her brother and a boy in their care in the family house near the center of the city to go take care of Georgia in this house. However, as the gunshots drew near, Jennie decided to join her mother and sister. So, she closed up their house and walked over with her brother and the other boy.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.ibafflatusdesign.space\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/07\/20180525_123709.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"On July 3rd, the third day of the battle, Jennie Wade woke up at 4am to knead enough bread for the soldiers and her family before the July heat became unbearable. She opened the parlor door as a bit of extra protection and began kneading behind it. Unfortunately, that day, a large bullet burst through the kitchen door and the parlor door and struck Jennie Wade in the back and pierced her heart. Jennie Wade was the only direct civilian casualty of the Battle of Gettysburg.\n&lt;p&gt;The bullet hole, pictured at around handle level between the two door panels, is said to bring marriage to any female who puts her finger through it. The framed letter on the door is of someone who claims to have put her finger through and to have been married shortly after. Personally, I don&#039;t see the connection between a hole that ended in someone&#039;s death and a superstition that leads to marriage but I thought it interesting nonetheless.&lt;\/p&gt;\" data-attachment-id=\"4027\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"On July 3rd, the third day of the battle, Jennie Wade woke up at 4am to knead enough bread for the soldiers and her family before the July heat became unbearable. She opened the parlor door as a bit of extra protection and began kneading behind it. Unfortunately, that day, a large bullet burst through the kitchen door and the parlor door and struck Jennie Wade in the back and pierced her heart. Jennie Wade was the only direct civilian casualty of the Battle of Gettysburg.\n&lt;p&gt;The bullet hole, pictured at around handle level between the two door panels, is said to bring marriage to any female who puts her finger through it. The framed letter on the door is of someone who claims to have put her finger through and to have been married shortly after. Personally, I don&#039;t see the connection between a hole that ended in someone&#039;s death and a superstition that leads to marriage but I thought it interesting nonetheless.&lt;\/p&gt;\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/www.ibafflatusdesign.space\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2018\/07\/20180525_123709\/127337269.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">On July 3rd, the third day of the battle, Jennie Wade woke up at 4am to knead enough bread for the soldiers and her family before the July heat became unbearable. She opened the parlor door as a bit of extra protection and began kneading behind it. Unfortunately, that day, a large bullet burst through the kitchen door and the parlor door and struck Jennie Wade in the back and pierced her heart. Jennie Wade was the only direct civilian casualty of the Battle of Gettysburg.\n<p>The bullet hole, pictured at around handle level between the two door panels, is said to bring marriage to any female who puts her finger through it. The framed letter on the door is of someone who claims to have put her finger through and to have been married shortly after. Personally, I don't see the connection between a hole that ended in someone's death and a superstition that leads to marriage but I thought it interesting nonetheless.<\/p><\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.ibafflatusdesign.space\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/07\/20180525_124225.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"At the sound of Jennie falling dead to the ground and the mother screaming once she saw what had happened, the soldiers came down from the second floor to see what had happened. At that point, the soldiers insisted that the family go hid out in the cellar. They couldn&#039;t leave through the front or kitchen door though because that&#039;s where the bullet had come from. One of the soldiers remembered that a large cannon bullet had barreled through the house earlier and had made a hole in the wall. The soldiers made the hole bigger (depicted here) and ushered the family into the adjoining part of the duplex house. Jennie&#039;s mother, though, insisted that she would not leave without both of her daughters. Therefore, the soldiers wrapped up Jennie&#039;s body and carried her upstairs as well. Once on the other side of the duplex, they went outside and down the outdoor stairs into the cellar, where they stayed until the end of the battle.\" data-attachment-id=\"4028\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"At the sound of Jennie falling dead to the ground and the mother screaming once she saw what had happened, the soldiers came down from the second floor to see what had happened. At that point, the soldiers insisted that the family go hid out in the cellar. They couldn&#039;t leave through the front or kitchen door though because that&#039;s where the bullet had come from. One of the soldiers remembered that a large cannon bullet had barreled through the house earlier and had made a hole in the wall. The soldiers made the hole bigger (depicted here) and ushered the family into the adjoining part of the duplex house. Jennie&#039;s mother, though, insisted that she would not leave without both of her daughters. Therefore, the soldiers wrapped up Jennie&#039;s body and carried her upstairs as well. Once on the other side of the duplex, they went outside and down the outdoor stairs into the cellar, where they stayed until the end of the battle.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/www.ibafflatusdesign.space\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2018\/07\/20180525_124225\/1369538498.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">At the sound of Jennie falling dead to the ground and the mother screaming once she saw what had happened, the soldiers came down from the second floor to see what had happened. At that point, the soldiers insisted that the family go hid out in the cellar. They couldn't leave through the front or kitchen door though because that's where the bullet had come from. One of the soldiers remembered that a large cannon bullet had barreled through the house earlier and had made a hole in the wall. The soldiers made the hole bigger (depicted here) and ushered the family into the adjoining part of the duplex house. Jennie's mother, though, insisted that she would not leave without both of her daughters. Therefore, the soldiers wrapped up Jennie's body and carried her upstairs as well. Once on the other side of the duplex, they went outside and down the outdoor stairs into the cellar, where they stayed until the end of the battle.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.ibafflatusdesign.space\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/07\/20180525_130447.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"This painting is called &quot;Through a Mother&#039;s Eyes&quot; as it depicts the situation from the point of view of the mother. (Jennie Wade is behind her sister laying covered on the cot, with one hand hanging out.\" data-attachment-id=\"4034\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"This painting is called &quot;Through a Mother&#039;s Eyes&quot; as it depicts the situation from the point of view of the mother. (Jennie Wade is behind her sister laying covered on the cot, with one hand hanging out.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/www.ibafflatusdesign.space\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2018\/07\/20180525_130447\/1563244408.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">This painting is called \"Through a Mother's Eyes\" as it depicts the situation from the point of view of the mother. (Jennie Wade is behind her sister laying covered on the cot, with one hand hanging out.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.ibafflatusdesign.space\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/07\/20180525_124422.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"This is the street side bedroom of the family that lived next door. The shoes left here were of average size for women in the day. They are a size 4.5.\n&lt;p&gt;The roller pin at the top of the bed frame was used to literally hit the hay, in order to spread it out and make it less bumpy. This made the bed more comfortable for sleeping. This has resulted in the expression &lt;i&gt;I&#039;m going to hit the hay.&lt;\/i&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Additionally, a replica of the cannon bullet, pictured in the left, is left where it would have been during the Battle of Gettysburg.&lt;\/p&gt;\" data-attachment-id=\"4029\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"This is the street side bedroom of the family that lived next door. The shoes left here were of average size for women in the day. They are a size 4.5.\n&lt;p&gt;The roller pin at the top of the bed frame was used to literally hit the hay, in order to spread it out and make it less bumpy. This made the bed more comfortable for sleeping. This has resulted in the expression &lt;i&gt;I&#039;m going to hit the hay.&lt;\/i&gt;&lt;\/p&gt;\n&lt;p&gt;Additionally, a replica of the cannon bullet, pictured in the left, is left where it would have been during the Battle of Gettysburg.&lt;\/p&gt;\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/www.ibafflatusdesign.space\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2018\/07\/20180525_124422\/207730369.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">This is the street side bedroom of the family that lived next door. The shoes left here were of average size for women in the day. They are a size 4.5.\n<p>The roller pin at the top of the bed frame was used to literally hit the hay, in order to spread it out and make it less bumpy. This made the bed more comfortable for sleeping. This has resulted in the expression <i>I'm going to hit the hay.<\/i><\/p>\n<p>Additionally, a replica of the cannon bullet, pictured in the left, is left where it would have been during the Battle of Gettysburg.<\/p><\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.ibafflatusdesign.space\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/07\/20180525_125046.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"\u2013 This is a picture of the well side bedroom. During the period of the Battle of Gettysburg, four children shared this one bed. The bed is kept from sagging by tightening the rope every couple of days. Hence the expression &lt;i&gt;sleep tight&lt;\/i&gt;. Moreover, it was the job of the youngest sibling to empty the chamber pots every morning.\" data-attachment-id=\"4031\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"\u2013 This is a picture of the well side bedroom. During the period of the Battle of Gettysburg, four children shared this one bed. The bed is kept from sagging by tightening the rope every couple of days. Hence the expression &lt;i&gt;sleep tight&lt;\/i&gt;. Moreover, it was the job of the youngest sibling to empty the chamber pots every morning.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/www.ibafflatusdesign.space\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2018\/07\/20180525_125046\/2610561241.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">\u2013 This is a picture of the well side bedroom. During the period of the Battle of Gettysburg, four children shared this one bed. The bed is kept from sagging by tightening the rope every couple of days. Hence the expression <i>sleep tight<\/i>. Moreover, it was the job of the youngest sibling to empty the chamber pots every morning.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.ibafflatusdesign.space\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/07\/20180525_125036.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"This is a panorama of the three rooms, as seen from the street side bedroom of the neighbor&#039;s house.\" data-attachment-id=\"4030\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"This is a panorama of the three rooms, as seen from the street side bedroom of the neighbor&#039;s house.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/www.ibafflatusdesign.space\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2018\/07\/20180525_125036\/2782977357.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">This is a panorama of the three rooms, as seen from the street side bedroom of the neighbor's house.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.ibafflatusdesign.space\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/07\/20180525_125408.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"In the living room of the neighbor&#039;s house is located a period piece containing some artifacts from the Jennie Wade house. For example, the original wood plank where Jennie bled out is on the middle shelf and the original cannon bullet is on the bottom shelf.\" data-attachment-id=\"4032\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"In the living room of the neighbor&#039;s house is located a period piece containing some artifacts from the Jennie Wade house. For example, the original wood plank where Jennie bled out is on the middle shelf and the original cannon bullet is on the bottom shelf.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/www.ibafflatusdesign.space\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2018\/07\/20180525_125408\/876295034.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">In the living room of the neighbor's house is located a period piece containing some artifacts from the Jennie Wade house. For example, the original wood plank where Jennie bled out is on the middle shelf and the original cannon bullet is on the bottom shelf.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.ibafflatusdesign.space\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/07\/20180525_125636.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"Downstairs in the neighbor&#039;s kitchen now hang three framed portraits of Jennie Wade and her two childhood friends. It is rumored that something of a love triangle resulted between the three friends but that Jennie Wade was engaged to Johnston Hastings Skelly. Johnston Skelly lived in Pennsylvania at the time and died a week after Jennie Wade on a field in Virginia. John Wesley Culp lived in Virginia at the outburst of the Civil War so he joined the Confederate Army. Culp died in the Battle of Gettysburg on his cousin&#039;s farm, on Culp&#039;s Hill.\" data-attachment-id=\"4033\" class=\"fg-thumb\"><span class=\"fg-image-wrap\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" title=\"Downstairs in the neighbor&#039;s kitchen now hang three framed portraits of Jennie Wade and her two childhood friends. It is rumored that something of a love triangle resulted between the three friends but that Jennie Wade was engaged to Johnston Hastings Skelly. Johnston Skelly lived in Pennsylvania at the time and died a week after Jennie Wade on a field in Virginia. John Wesley Culp lived in Virginia at the outburst of the Civil War so he joined the Confederate Army. Culp died in the Battle of Gettysburg on his cousin&#039;s farm, on Culp&#039;s Hill.\" width=\"150\" height=\"150\" class=\"skip-lazy fg-image\" data-src-fg=\"https:\/\/www.ibafflatusdesign.space\/wp-content\/uploads\/cache\/2018\/07\/20180525_125636\/1188199917.jpg\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml,%3Csvg%20xmlns%3D%22http%3A%2F%2Fwww.w3.org%2F2000%2Fsvg%22%20width%3D%22150%22%20height%3D%22150%22%20viewBox%3D%220%200%20150%20150%22%3E%3C%2Fsvg%3E\"><\/span><span class=\"fg-image-overlay\"><\/span><\/a><figcaption class=\"fg-caption\"><div class=\"fg-caption-inner\"><div class=\"fg-caption-title\">Downstairs in the neighbor's kitchen now hang three framed portraits of Jennie Wade and her two childhood friends. It is rumored that something of a love triangle resulted between the three friends but that Jennie Wade was engaged to Johnston Hastings Skelly. Johnston Skelly lived in Pennsylvania at the time and died a week after Jennie Wade on a field in Virginia. John Wesley Culp lived in Virginia at the outburst of the Civil War so he joined the Confederate Army. Culp died in the Battle of Gettysburg on his cousin's farm, on Culp's Hill.<\/div><\/div><\/figcaption><\/figure><div class=\"fg-loader\"><\/div><\/div><div class=\"fg-item fg-type-image fg-idle\"><figure class=\"fg-item-inner\"><a href=\"https:\/\/www.ibafflatusdesign.space\/wp-content\/uploads\/2018\/07\/20180525_130532.jpg\" data-caption-title=\"Behind the house, there is a well and a structure that houses the visitor&#039;s center. That structure was not there at the time but was built to look of the period.\" data-attachment-id=\"4035\" class=\"fg-thumb\"